    <div class="prose">
      <p>A website has one job for a tradesman: turn the person looking at it into an enquiry. Most don't. They're slow, they look like every other builder-template site, and the "contact us" is buried where nobody finds it. So the visitor bounces and rings the next name on Google instead.</p>
      <p>I build sites that do the opposite. Fast to load, clear on what you do, and pointed at one thing: getting that person to message you.</p>

      <h2>Hand-coded, not a drag-and-drop template</h2>
      <p>Every site I build is written by hand from scratch. Not Wix, not Squarespace, not a themed template with your logo dropped in the corner. That matters for three reasons a homeowner never sees but always feels:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Speed.</strong> Template builders load a pile of code you'll never use, which slows the page down. A slow site loses visitors before it's even finished loading, and Google ranks it lower for it. Hand-coded pages are lean and quick, especially on a phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Conversion.</strong> When I build every part myself, I build it around getting the enquiry, not around whatever a template designer thought looked nice. The layout, the buttons and the flow all point one way.</li>
        <li><strong>It's yours.</strong> No monthly builder subscription holding your site hostage, no locked-in platform. It looks and works exactly how you want because it's built for you, not rented.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What's included</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A fast, mobile-first site built around your trade and your brand</li>
        <li>Copy that says what you do and pushes the enquiry, in plain language</li>
        <li>Domain setup, so your site lives on your own web address</li>
        <li>Professional email setup on your domain, so you're not still on a hotmail address</li>
        <li>Clear enquiry routes: WhatsApp, call and message, wherever people actually want to reach you</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Bolt it onto your ads, or take it on its own</h2>
      <p>If you're running <a href="/services/facebook-lead-generation/">Facebook lead generation</a> with me, a proper site backs it up: people who see your ad and then look you up land somewhere that looks the part and closes the deal. But you don't have to run ads to get a site. Plenty of trades just want a clean, professional site that does them justice online, and that's a job on its own.</p>

      <h2>Recent work</h2>
      <p>Here's what one client said after I built theirs:</p>
